        skos:definition        "The pressure activation phase starts after the first successful auto-test and ends (with the start of the float mission) at the end of the CONFIG_PressureActivationTimeout_seconds period. During this phase the float checks the external pressure and can start its mission as soon as a CONFIG_PressureActivation_dbar pressure is measured. Template_Values:{unit:[days, hours, minutes, seconds, dsec, csec, msec, usec]}."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:R18::CC00143";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "CONFIG_PressureActivationTimeout_seconds"@en .

